users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-03T03:52:59Z","updated_at":"2025-10-03T03:52:59Z","body":"Some more features have been suggested here: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111118#issuecomment-3364154342\r\n```\r\ncv02 - Open four\r\ncv03 - Open six\r\ncv04 - Open nine (maybe leave nine closed or leave six closed?)\r\ncv05 - Lowercase L with tail\r\ncv08 - Uppercase I with serif\r\ncv09 - flat top three\r\ntnum - Evenly spaced numbers, makes the interface less \"jumpy\". (example gif on the original discussion)\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3364157832/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3364499568","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111140#issuecomment-3364499568","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111140","id":3364499568,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7IijBw","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-03T06:56:51Z","updated_at":"2025-10-03T06:59:32Z","body":"> Some more features have been suggested here: [#111118 (comment)](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111118#issuecomment-3364154342)\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> cv02 - Open four\r\n> cv03 - Open six\r\n> cv04 - Open nine (maybe leave nine closed or leave six closed?)\r\n> cv05 - Lowercase L with tail\r\n> cv08 - Uppercase I with serif\r\n> cv09 - flat top three\r\n> tnum - Evenly spaced numbers, makes the interface less \"jumpy\". (example gif on the original discussion)\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nI tested them before, and all of them showed the same [buggy hinting](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111140#issuecomment-3358640560) as serifed uppercase i.\r\n\r\nIf you look closely, the problem even happens with lowercase L, except it's barely noticeable until you compare with a lower or higher size.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3364499568/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3387863063","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111140#issuecomment-3387863063","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111140","id":3387863063,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7J7rAX","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-10T00:25:56Z","updated_at":"2025-10-10T23:05:42Z","body":"> One thing bothering me, however, is how hinting messes up alignment with uppercase i, making it look like it's out of place...\r\n\r\n> This doesn't happen if hinting is disabled, or the font size is 13 or 15. Maybe we should disable disambiguation for it and keep for lowercase L? They would end up different anyway.\r\n\r\nIn case we want those other variations, #111461 is mandatory.\r\n\r\n**EDIT**: Apparently not, in case we use font feature freeze.\r\n\r\nOn the other hand, doing so implies modifying the font, which requires copyright info modification by the terms of OFL (at least Adwaita Sans, which *is* a font feature freeze by GNOME that only enables a character variant, does that). \r\n\r\nWith that said, I think it's better to wait for HarfBuzz auto-hinting.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3387863063/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3393405607","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111140#issuecomment-3393405607","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111140","id":3393405607,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KQ0Kn","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-11T15:03:30Z","updated_at":"2025-10-11T16:05:36Z","body":"> There's also Adwaita Mono (a customized Iosevka) which could replace JetBrains Mono, as it's designed to pair well with Adwaita Sans.\r\n\r\nOfftopic but, if we truly want a customized Iosevka, the best variant would probably be Iosevka SS14 Extended, which is customized to look like JetBrains Mono.\r\n\r\nOn the other hand, JetBrains Mono's WOFF2 file is 90.2KiB, while the average pre-compiled Iosevka WOFF2 won't be lower than 300 KiB. And comparing, I personally don't see any advantages.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3393405607/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3399655785","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111140#issuecomment-3399655785","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111140","id":3399655785,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KoqFp","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-14T01:41:20Z","updated_at":"2025-10-15T02:02:25Z","body":"With the issue with variant hinting gone, I have re-enabled serif uppercase i and slashed 0. Added more screenshots to the main comment.\r\n\r\nThe [proposal](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/discussions/9012) suggests `ss01` (all alternate digits), `ss04` (I and l disambiguation without slashed 0) and `tnum` (tabular numbers). But for now, I'll just let the default disambiguation in unless someone really wants something else.\r\n\r\nIf anyone disagrees with slashed 0, we can just replace `ss02` with `ss04`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3399655785/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3407697757","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111140#issuecomment-3407697757","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111140","id":3407697757,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LHVdd","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-15T18:13:03Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T18:52:19Z","body":"Decided to showcase variant candidates separately.\r\n\r\n`ss01` (alternate digits):\r\n<img width=\"294\" height=\"85\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4706ad39-8d67-4428-8612-663b9b9e6e15\" />\r\n\r\n`ss02` (serifed I, tailed l and slashed zero):\r\n<img width=\"288\" height=\"80\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3545cb35-1c4f-48c6-912f-6dc07596c3c5\" />\r\n\r\n`ss04` (same as `ss02` but without slashed zero):\r\n<img width=\"294\" height=\"79\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/912e92ea-0c86-4327-bc12-e64d144c92a4\" />\r\n\r\n`tnum` (tabular numbers):\r\n<img width=\"300\" height=\"86\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/51910f62-ce60-4658-b750-be6c8b80317d\" />\r\n\r\n`ss01` + `ss02`:\r\n<img width=\"296\" height=\"88\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9800ad10-3bf4-44bd-b4c3-230e75694a96\" />\r\n\r\n`ss01` + `tnum`:\r\n<img width=\"285\" height=\"80\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bdbd8212-42d7-472d-9ff3-dc60684b2a50\" />\r\n\r\n`ss02` + `tnum`:\r\n<img width=\"293\" height=\"79\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e6d7ea1a-34ba-4c1e-9282-559ad344e17a\" />\r\n\r\n`ss04` + `tnum` (***current candidate***):\r\n<img width=\"305\" height=\"84\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7775b5e0-9f0a-4e06-8a95-4de479e40563\" />\r\n\r\n`ss01` + `ss02` + `tnum`:\r\n<img width=\"291\" height=\"86\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/469b15b5-5470-4396-a49e-6e4a06a62195\" />\r\n\r\nMy personal opinion: \r\n- Uppercase i being serifed makes it closer to Noto Sans' which is serifed by default.\r\n- Either serifed uppercase i, or tailed lowercase L, or both, are desired, as the defaults are literally the same character.\r\n- Slashed zero only serves to further differentiate it from uppercase o. Fonts like JetBrains Mono do this by default, although with a dot in the middle instead of a slash. Could be desired too.\r\n- Tabular numbers might make number fields more consistent. Float sliders benefit from this.\r\n- Alternate digits is pretty much a stylistic choice, but could be better for reading due to looking unique compared to every other character.\r\n\r\nIf anyone else has a preference, I'm interested in hearing it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3407697757/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3408622198","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111140#issuecomment-3408622198","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111140","id":3408622198,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LK3J2","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-15T23:24:29Z","updated_at":"2025-10-15T23:25:28Z","body":"I would go for `ss02` + `tnum` personally. Tabular (= fixed-width) numbers will make many places in the editor look more consistent when values change, such as the **View Information** and **View Frame Time** panels in the 3D editor.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3408622198/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3416739332","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111140#issuecomment-3416739332","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111140","id":3416739332,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Lp04E","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-17T19:00:36Z","updated_at":"2025-10-17T19:01:04Z","body":"I personally don't like the slashed zero! I feel like there's very few places in the editor where the distinction between `0` and `O` matters, because the editor itself (outside of code) generally avoids this ambiguity. For example, \"text\" and \"numbers\" tend to be distinct from one another, and very few properties have a `0` in their names (and it hardly can be confused for a lone letter). With little benefit, the slash only makes the zero noisier.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3416739332/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3416770427","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111140#issuecomment-3416770427","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111140","id":3416770427,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Lp8d7","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-17T19:10:32Z","updated_at":"2025-10-17T19:10:32Z","body":"Stuff like slashed zero probably should be configurable, we have editor option to set OpenType feature tags for the code font, so no reason not to have one for main font as well (but UI should be improved, currently it's just a text field).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3416770427/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3416815416","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111140#issuecomment-3416815416","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111140","id":3416815416,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LqHc4","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-17T19:25:32Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T20:57:52Z","body":"I have updated so it only applies `I` and `l` disambiguation + tabular numbers for now. Slashed 0 removed.\r\n\r\n~~If I were to add an option to set OpenType feature tags for the main font *now*, it would probably go beyond the scope of this PR. Tabular numbers would be quite easy to do as a drop down like `code_font_contextual_ligatures` as it has a predefined name.~~ Edit: there is a Main Font Custom OpenType Features setting now.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3416815416/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3417034760","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111140#issuecomment-3417034760","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111140","id":3417034760,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Lq9AI","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-17T20:31:39Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T20:10:32Z","body":"> Stuff like slashed zero probably should be configurable, we have editor option to set OpenType feature tags for the code font, so no reason not to have one for main font as well (but UI should be improved, currently it's just a text field).\r\n\r\nAs I investigated further, turns out Inter does have a `calt` enabled by default. Maybe it's better we do it first.\r\n\r\nFor context, JetBrains Mono's `calt` is enabled in the font file, but it gets disabled by default in the editor settings.\r\n\r\nEdit: opened at #111773\r\n\r\nEdit 2: disabled `calt` on Inter by default in this PR, much like it's done with JetBrains Mono. #111773 would be needed to enable it again.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3417034760/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"outdated"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3428953831","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111140#issuecomment-3428953831","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111140","id":3428953831,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MYa7n","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-21T19:05:55Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T20:46:24Z","body":"As a follow-u